# Module content

Validate module metadata against `content/schema/module.schema.json`. Keep `module.yaml` as the machine-readable record; keep lesson Markdown free of answer keys.

A module is not publishable unless it (blueprint §16):

1. begins with a security property or question;
2. names attacker capabilities and trust assumptions;
3. distinguishes root cause, exploit preconditions, impact, prevention, detection, and recovery;
4. uses current canonical standards and labels maturity/status;
5. explains mechanism limits and common failure modes;
6. includes a safe practice task and a transfer task;
7. tests forbidden outcomes and failure behavior;
8. separates framework defaults from application guarantees;
9. avoids universal claims where risk-based selection is required;
10. contains no live-target instructions or real sensitive data;
11. has executable code/labs verified in a clean environment (Pass B+);
12. tests usability/accessibility of security-sensitive journeys where humans are part of the control;
13. records reviewer and review date.

Required fields include misconceptions, invariants, evidence, standards refs with version/status/url, and operational considerations.

Answer keys belong only in `content/assessment/keys/`.
